# Where the browser sends API calls.
#
# Leave this unset (or commented out) when running `npm run dev`: Vite's dev proxy
# forwards /api and /uploads to http://localhost:5000, so a relative path just works.
#
# Leave this unset for normal use, locally and in production. In development Vite's
# proxy forwards /api and /uploads to http://localhost:5000, and in production
# vercel.json forwards them to the API host, so the same relative path works in both.
#
# Only give it a value to aim a build at some other backend:
#   VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:5000/api
#
# Vite reads this while *building*, not at runtime, so a value here is frozen into the
# bundle and outranks the relative default — which is how a stale address once broke
# sign-in on the live site. If the site should talk to the API through its own domain,
# this variable must be absent, not merely correct.
VITE_API_URL=
